3-12-06"}}, {"rank": 4, "chunk_id": "09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856:52", "distance": 0.8705621957778931, "metadata": {"chunk_index": 52, "chunk_id": "09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856:52", "chunk_len_words": 512, "source_url": "https://www.parliament.gh/epanel/docs/pb/19th February, 2025.pdf", "title": "Hansard 19th February, 2025", "doc_id": "Hansard 19th February, 2025", "pdf_path": "data/corpus/clean/pdfs/2025-02-19 - Hansard 19th February 2025.pdf", "date_iso": "2025-02-19", "sha256_pdf": "09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856"}}, {"rank": 5, "chunk_id": "dfb854d2e036ec0d7e95b53e94c88bfc469f0184a4bc76853bf8d865ecd5540c:7", "distance": 0.8739883899688721, "metadata": {"chunk_len_words": 512, "date_iso": "2023-12-04", "chunk_index": 7, "doc_id": "Hansard 4th December, 2023", "sha256_pdf": "dfb854d2e036ec0d7e95b53e94c88bfc469f0184a4bc76853bf8d865ecd5540c", "source_url": "https://www.parliament.gh/epanel/docs/pb/4th December, 2023.pdf", "chunk_id": "dfb854d2e036ec0d7e95b53e94c88bfc469f0184a4bc76853bf8d865ecd5540c:7", "title": "Hansard 4th December, 2023", "pdf_path": "data/corpus/clean/pdfs/2023-12-04 - Hansard 4th December 2023.pdf"}}]}, "prev_hash": "56dbe5901a1c7206be1b4873334ce97c866f736e787a4e84a64e102e1699fb87", "event_hash": "29d44e03d0a058742dabbc999f82461b95d2fc3ee3486fdb19d0b493b426f476"}
{"ts_utc": "2026-05-13T11:37:12.145649Z", "run_id": "20260513_113652_rag_L3_S_I2_aae5ed", "seq": 5, "event": "generation.completed", "payload": {"answer": "Parliament did not explicitly state its opinion on education policy in general. However, they discussed specific issues related to the Free Senior High School (FSHS) Programme and its impact on education.\n\nThe FSHS Programme was mentioned as a flagship programme of the previous Government that had both positive and negative effects on education [09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856:52]. Some Members of Parliament, such as Dr. Ato-Forson, expressed concerns about the programme's impact on quality education and the perceived climate of fear and intimidation among school administrators [2fc50d4e2a88b6bf595eef06a7e0ea916fc876c9f0060a7868a860ee4fe7bf99:44].\n\nOn the other hand, Dr. Mahama praised the programme for taking away the financial burden of education from parents and making it compulsory for every child to attend school [09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856:52].\n\nRegarding specific policy decisions, Parliament decided that the Hon Minister for Education should come to the Floor of the House and present a Statement on the matter [2fc50d4e2a88b6bf595eef06a7e0ea916fc876c9f0060a7868a860ee4fe7bf99:22].", "answer_sha256": "e2ee91bd30b0c349b50f5dae5581ae0a09c14dc2c4b595f79fea2dd4ddf704f1"}, "prev_hash": "29d44e03d0a058742dabbc999f82461b95d2fc3ee3486fdb19d0b493b426f476", "event_hash": "4dedb348a0dd0a1a2b3fb637d4afd4b1c1dddff1c33f90e1c62a2a6368cdb40d"}
